[{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q1","number":1,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The system is released from rest. In each case find the tension in the string and the acceleration of the system:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=9\\text{ kg},m_B=3\\text{ kg}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=2\\text{ kg},m_B=8\\text{ kg}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=200\\text{ g},m_B=500\\text{ g}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9\\times9.8-T=9a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-3\\times9.8=3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=44.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.9\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=44\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.9\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-2\\times9.8=2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\\times9.8-T=8a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=31.36\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5.88\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=32\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5.9\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-0.2\\times9.8=0.2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\times9.8-T=0.5a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=2.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>the tension in the string in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>the magnitude of the force exerted on the pulley while <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are in motion.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5m\\times9.8-T=5ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-3m\\times9.8=3ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Adding the equations:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"49m-T+T-29.4m=8ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"49-29.4=8a\\Rightarrow a=2.45\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=36.75m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2T=73.5m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q3","number":3,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use exact values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M&gt;m\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest. The tension in the string is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N and the acceleration is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a=\\left(\\frac{M-m}{M+m}\\right)g\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-mg=ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Mg-T=Ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Adding the equations:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Mg-T+T-mg=ma+Ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(M-m)g=(M+m)a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow a=\\left(\\frac{M-m}{M+m}\\right)g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"km\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. They are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest. The acceleration of the system is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a=\\left(\\frac{k-1}{k+1}\\right)g\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"kmg-T=kma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-mg=ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Adding the equations:</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"kmg-T+T-mg=kma+ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"kg-g=ka+a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(k-1)=a(k+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\left(\\frac{k-1}{k+1}\\right)g\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q5","number":5,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.81\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has mass 2 kg and descends 0.8 metres in the first 4 seconds after the system is released. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>the tension in the string.</p></li><li><p>the mass of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.8=0+\\frac12a\\times4^2\\Rightarrow a=0.1\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times9.81-T=2\\times0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow T=19.42\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=19.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (3 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"19.42-m\\times9.81=m\\times0.1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow m=1.96\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Two particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of masses 4 kg and 3 kg respectively are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q6.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest. Initially, particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> begins 1.5 metres above the ground.</p><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>the tension in the string.</p></li><li><p>the time it takes for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to hit the ground.</p></li><li><p>the greatest height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> above the floor, stating any modelling assumptions you have made.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\times9.81-T=4a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-3\\times9.81=3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{981}{700}=1.40\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=\\frac{5886}{175}=33.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.5=0+\\frac12\\times\\frac{981}{700}\\times t^2\\Rightarrow t=1.46\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=0+2\\times\\frac{981}{700}\\times1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow v=\\sqrt{\\frac{2943}{700}}=2.050435494\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hits the ground, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> continues upwards until it slows to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=u^2+2as\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=\\frac{2943}{700}+2\\times-9.81s\\Rightarrow s=\\frac3{14}=0.2142857\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Therefore 1.71 metres above the floor.</p>","<p>Modelling assumptions: there are no resistances to motion (such as friction or air resistance), the pulley is small, particle B does not hit the pulley.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q7","number":7,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong></p><p>Two boxes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of masses 5 kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a smooth small fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut, and the system is released from rest.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q7.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> starts 0.5 metres above the ground.</p><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> ascends 0.2 metres in the first 0.5 seconds after the system is released.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>Find the tension in the string.</p></li><li><p>Show that the mass of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is approximately 7 kg.</p></li><li><p>Find the velocity at which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hits the ground.</p></li></ol><p>Once Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hits the ground, the string holding up box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> becomes slack.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"5\"><li><p>Given box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> starts 1 metre above the ground, find the greatest height that box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> reaches above the ground.</p></li><li><p>Find the time box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> spends with the string not taut.</p></li></ol><p>A different box (box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>) is attached to the string, in replacement of box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The system is re-set so that Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> starts 0.5 m above the ground.</p><p>Explain what box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> will experience with its acceleration (including the direction) and the tension in the string in each of the following scenarios:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"7\"><li><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a larger mass than box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has the same mass as box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a lower mass than box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.2=0+\\frac12a\\times0.5^2\\Rightarrow a=1.6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-5\\times9.8=5\\times1.6\\Rightarrow T=57\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\\times9.8-57=m\\times1.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow m=\\frac{285}{41}=6.951219512\\approx7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg as required.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v^2=0+2\\times1.6\\times0.5\\Rightarrow v=\\frac25\\sqrt{10}=1.26\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=1.6+2\\times-9.8\\times s\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow s=\\frac4{49}=0.08163265306\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+0.5+0.08163\\ldots=1.58163\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Therefore 1.58 metres above the floor.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=\\frac25\\sqrt{10}t+\\frac12\\times-9.8\\times t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.2581451151\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So 0.258 seconds</p>","<p>0.26 seconds (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> will ascend with a higher acceleration and there will be a higher tension in the string.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">h)</h3><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> will not move as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and so the tension will be equal to the weight of box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">i)</h3><p>Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> will descend and there will be a lower tension in the string.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Two boxes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of masses 3 kg and 0.5 kg respectively are attached to the end of a light inextensible string which passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The system is released from rest. Box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> begins <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres from the ground and box <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> begins <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres from the ground.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>the tension in the string.</p></li><li><p>Show that the time after release that both boxes are at the same height is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"t=\\sqrt{\\frac{4h}7}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\times9.8-T=3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-0.5\\times9.8=0.5a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=7\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=8.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=0+\\frac12\\times7\\times t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=3.5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Distance of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow2h=3.5t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac47h=t^2\\Rightarrow t=\\sqrt{\\frac{4h}7}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds as req.</p>","<p>(Time must be positive)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A scale pan <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg hangs freely and is attached by a light inextensible string to a mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is 8 kg. The string passes over a small smooth fixed pulley. The masses hang with the string taut.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q9.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>An object of mass 2 kg is placed into the scale pan and the system is released from rest. The scale pan <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> descends but doesn't exceed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.96\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the range of the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N is the tension in the string.</p></li><li><p>the range of values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-8\\times9.8=8\\times1.96\\Rightarrow T=94.08\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-8\\times9.8=0\\Rightarrow T=78.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"78.4&lt;T\\le94.08\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"78&lt;T\\le94\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m&gt;6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(m+2)\\times9.8-94.08=(m+2)\\times1.96\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9.8m+19.6-94.08=1.96m+3.92\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7.84m=78.4\\Rightarrow m=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6&lt;m\\le10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Two particles, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have masses 1.2 kg and 0.5 kg respectively. They are connected by a light, inextensible string. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on a smooth horizontal table and the string passes over a small round smooth pulley which is fixed at the edge of a table. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hangs freely.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q10.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>the tension in the string.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=1.2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\times9.8-T=0.5a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{49}{17}=2.88\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2.9\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=3.46\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=3.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Two particles, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively. They are connected by a light, inextensible string. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on a rough horizontal table and the string passes over a small round pulley which is fixed at the edge of a table. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hangs freely. The resistance force acting on particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The system is released from rest.</p><p>Find, in each case, the acceleration of the system and the tension in the string.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=2\\text{ kg},m_B=3\\text{ kg},F=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=5\\text{ kg},m_B=7\\text{ kg},F=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=200\\text{ g},m_B=500\\text{ g},F=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m_A=8\\text{ kg},m_B=6\\text{ kg},F=58.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-20=2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\times9.8-T=3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=1.88\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=23.76\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=1.9\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=24\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-12=5a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7\\times9.8-T=7a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.72\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=35.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.7\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=36\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-2=0.2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\times9.8-T=0.5a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.14\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=2.83\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=4.1\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=2.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-58.8=8a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\times9.8-T=6a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=58.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=59\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>For each of the scenarios in question 11), find the time it takes for particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to travel 1 m, assuming particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> begins over 1 metre from the floor.</p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1=0+\\frac12\\times\\frac{47}{25}\\times t^2\\Rightarrow t=1.03\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1.0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1=0+\\frac12\\times\\frac{283}{60}\\times t^2\\Rightarrow t=0.651\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.65\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1=0+\\frac12\\times\\frac{29}7\\times t^2\\Rightarrow t=0.695\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0.69\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The system does not move</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q13","number":13,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=10\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong></p><p>A van <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of mass 2000 kg is attached with a cable to a pallet of building materials <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which has mass 100 kg. The cable passes over a smooth fixed pulley, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hangs freely.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q13.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Initially the system is at rest and the cable is taut. The van begins to drive away from the pulley with driving force 2500 N. The resistance force acting on the van is 450 N.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>Find the tension in the cable.</p></li><li><p>State two modelling assumptions that you have made.</p></li></ol><p>The van drives forward for 10 seconds before the pallet is getting close to reaching the pulley.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li><p>Find the height that the pallet has been lifted.</p></li><li><p>State any assumptions in you have used.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\leftarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2500-450-T=2000a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-100\\times10=100a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=1050\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=1000\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The cable is light and inextensible. The pulley is small.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=0+\\frac12\\times0.5\\times10^2=25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>No resistances acting against the pallet of building materials.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>Two particles, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively. They are connected by a light, inextensible string. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on a smooth horizontal table and the string passes over a small round smooth pulley which is fixed at the edge of a table. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hangs freely.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q14.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{10m}{m+M}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=Ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10m-T=ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T+10m-T=Ma+ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10m=(m+M)a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{10m}{m+M}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q15","number":15,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong></p><p>A wooden block <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with mass 300 g sits on a rough table, attached to a string which passes over a small, smooth pulley which is fixed to the edge of the table. A plastic block <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg hangs freely at the end of the string.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q15.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The system is released from rest and block <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> descends. The resistance to motion on block <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 5 N.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration of the system in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The block <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> initially starts 1.2 metres above the ground. It takes 2 seconds for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to reach the ground.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>State any modelling assumptions you have made.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-5=0.3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9.8m-T=ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5+9.8m=0.3a+ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5+9.8m=a(0.3+m)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{9.8m-5}{m+0.3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.2=0+\\frac12a\\times4\\Rightarrow a=0.6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5+9.8m=0.3\\times0.6+0.6m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9.2m=5.18\\Rightarrow m=\\frac{259}{460}=0.563\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=0.56\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>There are no resistances to motion on block <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>Particles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, have masses 2 kg, 8 kg and 3 kg respectively. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are attached to the ends of a light inextensible string. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are attached to the ends of another light inextensible string. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> rests on a smooth table. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hang freely. Both strings pass over small smooth fixed pulleys at the edge of the table with the string taut.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q16.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The system is released from rest. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the system.</p></li><li><p>the tension in the two strings.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>On <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\leftarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1-T_2=2a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8\\times9.8-T_1=8a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2-3\\times9.8=3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{49}{13}=3.77\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=3.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2 SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1=\\frac{3136}{65}=48.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=\\frac{2646}{65}=40.7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N,</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_1=48\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T_2=41\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2 SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q17","number":17,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use exact values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong></p><p>Two particles, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"km\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. They are connected by a light, inextensible string. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on a rough horizontal table and the string passes over a small round smooth pulley which is fixed at the edge of a table. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hangs freely.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q17.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The system is released from rest.</p><p>The resistance to motion on particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12kmg\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N. Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{kg}{2(1+k)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\rightarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-\\frac12kmg=ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\downarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"kmg-T=kma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T+kmg-T-\\frac12kmg=ma+kma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12kmg=(1+k)ma\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12kg=(1+k)a\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=\\frac{kg}{2(1+k)}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as req.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.70-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>Two particles, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have masses <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"km\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg respectively where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. They are connected by a light, inextensible string. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on a rough horizontal table and the string passes over a small round smooth pulley which is fixed at the edge of a table. Particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> hangs freely.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.70/questions/assets/diagrams/q18.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>A horizontal force of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N is applied to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> away from the pulley. The resistance to motion on particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10mg\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N. Initially at rest, particle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> travels 0.5 m in 10 s.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration of the system</p></li><li><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{1000g-3}{100g+1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5=0+\\frac12a\\times100\\Rightarrow a=0.01\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On A <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\leftarrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20mg-T-10mg=0.03m\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>On B <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R(\\uparrow)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T-kmg=0.01km\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20mg-T-10mg+T-kmg=0.03m+0.01km\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20g-10g-kg=0.03+0.01k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10g-0.03=kg+0.01k\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10g-0.03=k(g+0.01)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac{10g-0.03}{g+0.01}=\\frac{1000g-3}{100g+1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]}]